WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.867 --> 00:00:12.567
The person in the water turned out to be a boy.

2
00:00:12.568 --> 00:00:15.833
He was holding a large basket of mud.

3
00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:21.224
Coughing, Vinnie climbed back onto the tiny island.

4
00:00:21.225 --> 00:00:24.468
“Who are you?” the boy asked.

5
00:00:24.469 --> 00:00:28.109
“I’m Vinnie. This is my sister, Mandy,”

6
00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:33.480
Vinnie replied, shaking his wet hair.

7
00:00:33.481 --> 00:00:37.849
“Where is your family garden?” the boy asked.

8
00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:42.091
“We don’t have one,” admitted Vinnie.

9
00:00:42.092 --> 00:00:43.742
“We’re just visiting.

10
00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:46.094
Do you need help?”

11
00:00:46.095 --> 00:00:48.698
The boy thought a moment.

12
00:00:48.699 --> 00:00:51.083
“Yes,” he said.

13
00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:53.191
“Collect mud from the lake.

14
00:00:53.192 --> 00:00:55.537
Then pile it on here.”

15
00:00:55.538 --> 00:00:59.171
He pointed to the island.

16
00:00:59.172 --> 00:01:02.941
He had dark skin and was dressed like Vinnie.

17
00:01:02.942 --> 00:01:06.947
“Why do you need mud?” Vinnie asked.

18
00:01:06.948 --> 00:01:10.288
The boy looked at them, surprised.

19
00:01:10.289 --> 00:01:14.073
“It helps the crops grow strong,” he said.

20
00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:17.285
“Corn and beans grow best on this soil.

21
00:01:17.286 --> 00:01:20.278
Our corn was very good last year.

22
00:01:20.279 --> 00:01:24.423
So we are making more floating gardens.”

23
00:01:24.424 --> 00:01:27.042
“What a great name!”

24
00:01:27.043 --> 00:01:29.142
Mandy clapped her hands.

25
00:01:29.143 --> 00:01:33.424
The tiny islands did look like floating gardens.

26
00:01:33.425 --> 00:01:36.084
Each one had a different crop.

27
00:01:36.085 --> 00:01:42.426
For the next hour, Vinnie and Mandy helped the boy.

28
00:01:42.427 --> 00:01:45.334
They piled mud on the island.

29
00:01:45.335 --> 00:01:48.269
Mandy smoothed the mud with a stick.

30
00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:50.676
A canoe went by.

31
00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:53.738
“Look, Vinnie!” she called.

32
00:01:53.739 --> 00:01:59.727
“People use canoes to move from one island to the next.”

33
00:01:59.728 --> 00:02:04.028
“Who are you, little girl?” someone behind her asked.

34
00:02:04.029 --> 00:02:06.273
Mandy turned around.

35
00:02:06.274 --> 00:02:10.883
A man was sitting in a canoe with a big pile of corn.

36
00:02:10.884 --> 00:02:12.950
He had kind eyes.

37
00:02:12.951 --> 00:02:16.550
“We’re friends of . . .” Mandy paused.

38
00:02:16.551 --> 00:02:20.755
She didn’t know the boy’s name.

39
00:02:20.756 --> 00:02:23.545
“Of Mazatl? I see.

40
00:02:23.546 --> 00:02:26.618
Where is my son now?” he asked.

41
00:02:26.619 --> 00:02:31.340
“He’s getting mud from the water, sir,” she replied.

42
00:02:31.341 --> 00:02:36.135
Mandy thought Mazatl looked very much like his father.

43
00:02:36.136 --> 00:02:39.538
“Good,” Mazatl’s father nodded.

44
00:02:39.539 --> 00:02:42.201
“Tell Mazatl I will be at the market.

45
00:02:42.202 --> 00:02:45.417
I want to go early to get a good spot.”

46
00:02:45.418 --> 00:02:47.839
He paddled away.

47
00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:51.236
As Mandy watched him leave, she wondered,

48
00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:53.817
“Where are we?”

49
00:02:53.818 --> 00:02:59.739
When the boys returned, Mandy told Mazatl what his father said.

50
00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:04.803
“I must hurry and join Papa at the weekly market,” said Mazatl.

51
00:03:04.804 --> 00:03:08.443
“May we come with you?” asked Vinnie.

52
00:03:08.444 --> 00:03:12.481
“Yes, but come to my house first,” said Mazatl.

53
00:03:12.482 --> 00:03:17.354
“We can take a bath and change our clothes.”

54
00:03:17.355 --> 00:03:20.412
“Thanks, Mazatl,” Mandy said.

55
00:03:20.413 --> 00:03:23.742
“What a great place this is.”

56
00:03:23.743 --> 00:03:25.457
Mazatl nodded.

57
00:03:25.458 --> 00:03:29.118
She really wished she knew where she was.

58
00:03:29.119 --> 00:03:34.137
“Our gods are good to us if we are good to them,” Mazatl said.

59
00:03:34.138 --> 00:03:38.934
“How are you good to the gods?” Mandy asked.

60
00:03:38.935 --> 00:03:41.881
“We make sacrifices regularly.”

61
00:03:41.882 --> 00:03:47.626
“What kind of sacrifices?” asked Vinnie.

62
00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:50.832
Mazatl stared at them suspiciously.

63
00:03:50.833 --> 00:03:59.371
“Our Aztec gods are offered only the best sacrifices—humans!” he said proudly.

64
00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:06.154
“Aztec? We’re in ancient Mexico?” gasped Mandy.

65
00:04:06.155 --> 00:04:12.918
“Human sacrifices?” cried Vinnie.
